<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Khanwa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Khanwa was fought in 1527 in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babur">Babur</a> and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> confederacy led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rana-sanga">Rana Sanga</a> of Mewar. Babur's forces, using <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">field artillery</a> and firearms, won a decisive victory. It secured Babur's position in northern India and consolidated the foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-khanwa.jpg" alt="Battle of Khanwa" width="251" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: &quot;Mirza 'Abd al-Rahim, Khan-i khanan (Mirza 'Abd al-Rahim, Khan-i khanan)&quot; · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Babur%E2%80%99s_army_in_battle_against_the_army_of_Rana_Sanga_at.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
